# DC-36
C('D-36', S, 'Design: Change Customer warns when a vendor bill was already posted',
  ['Sign in as an Admin (a user with every setting, See Financial Data included).', 'Use a desktop browser window 1440 pixels wide at 100% zoom.', 'Have Internal Work Orders turned on in Settings > Work Orders.', 'Use a location that is connected to QuickBooks Online, with every ShopView Accounts row mapped.', 'Have a customer flagged as Internal customer, with one asset, and its default internal category left at General Internal.', 'Have a regular customer (not flagged), with one asset.', 'Have a new billable work order for the regular customer with a special-order part whose vendor bill is posted, made for this test.', 'Open the attached pictures iwo-flow1-05-2c-change-customer-bill-already-posted.png, iwo-flow1-06-2d-change-customer-bill-already-posted.png at 100% zoom beside the screen.'],
  ['Open the billable work order.', 'Click Change Customer on the customer card.', 'Pick the internal customer.'],
  [['The work order opens.'], ['The customer picker opens.'], ['A window "Change where the cost is posted?" opens with the body "The vendor bill for [part] ($[amount]) was posted to Cost of Parts. If you continue, that cost moves to [expense account of General Internal] when this work order is closed."', 'Buttons Cancel then "Continue".']],
  ['S2-R8'],
  note="Words in square brackets in a message stand for the value they name, such as the work order's number or the customer's name exactly as it is saved; every other word of the message must match exactly.",
  stories=[2])
