# DV-02
C('D-88', S, 'Design: Open internal work order estimate carries the INTERNAL stamp',
  ['Sign in as an Admin (a user with every setting, See Financial Data included).', 'Use a desktop browser window 1440 pixels wide at 100% zoom.', 'Have Internal Work Orders turned on in Settings > Work Orders.', 'Have a customer flagged as Internal customer, with one asset, and its default internal category left at General Internal.', 'Have a new internal work order for that customer and asset, with one labor line (1.0 h) and one stock part with a cost (for example $95.00), the line In Progress, made for this test.', 'Open the attached pictures iwo-flow1-12-04-work-order-finance-tab.png, iwo-happy-15-15-finance-tab.png at 100% zoom beside the screen.'],
  ['Open the internal work order.', 'Click the Finance tab.'],
  [['The work order opens.'], ['The estimate carries the INTERNAL stamp with "Category: General Internal" under it (the design version).']],
  [('S2-R4', 'The estimate and invoice documents for these work orders show the same and carry the NO CHARGE stamp and, on a no-charge work order, the line "Category: [Category]" under the stamp; the shop-floor Print Work Order is unchanged (it carries no prices today).'), ('S3-R5', 'The Finance tab of a closed work order shows the NO CHARGE document: the masthead as on the invoice today (letterhead left, the shop logo in the centre slot, the document block "Internal Work Order [number]" or "No Charge Work Order [number]" with the date right), and under the masthead line, on the left and never over the logo, the INTERNAL or NO CHARGE stamp with the line "Category: [name]" and, when set, "· Original work order [number]" (a link in ShopView, plain on the PDF), Bill to the customer, the asset block, labor lines with hours only, parts lines with quantity and cost only (cost under \'See Financial Data\'), a Summary with Parts cost (one number: stock parts plus special orders and sublet, at the amounts of S3-R2, core cost excluded, S2-E7), Shop supplies (when above $0.00) and Labor hours (the labor hours on the lines), and no tax, total, payments, balance or signature block; with Download, Print and Email (the recipient field is empty; the user types the shop\'s own address or any other; never automatically).')],
  marker='AUTOMATION: HOLD - the design differs from the PRD, waiting on the PO (question 3)',
  stories=[2, 3])
# DV-03
C('D-89', S, 'Design: Closed internal work order shows the locked note',
  ['Sign in as an Admin (a user with every setting, See Financial Data included).', 'Use a desktop browser window 1440 pixels wide at 100% zoom.', 'Have Internal Work Orders turned on in Settings > Work Orders.', 'Have a customer flagged as Internal customer, with one asset, and its default internal category left at General Internal.', 'Have a closed internal work order, made for this test.', 'Open the attached pictures iwo-flow3-02-02-reopen-dialog.png, iwo-happy-37-37-reopen-work-order.png at 100% zoom beside the screen.'],
  ['Open the closed internal work order.'],
  [['A note reads "Closed on [date] by [user]", "This work order is locked. Reopen it to change lines, hours or parts." and "Reopening returns it from Closed · Internal to Complete." (the design version).']],
  [('S2-R9', 'From Close or invoice on, the classification and the category are locked: a closed no-charge work order shows the No Charge badge with no Convert or Change category action, on a closed internal or no-charge work order the Change Customer button on the customer card is disabled with the tooltip "Reopen the work order to change the customer." (the lock an invoiced or paid billable work order has today, S2-R7), and the header card carries the line "Closed on [posting date]. To change it, reopen it from the Finance tab."')],
  marker='AUTOMATION: HOLD - the design differs from the PRD, waiting on the PO (question 13)',
  note="Words in square brackets in a message stand for the value they name, such as the work order's number or the customer's name exactly as it is saved; every other word of the message must match exactly.",
  stories=[2, 4])
